<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Date</h1>
<p>Time in Valhalla runs 12 times faster than real time:
</p>
<pre>1 hour   =  5 real minutes
1 day    =  24 hours  =  2 real hours
1 month  =  14 days   =  28 real hours
1 year   =  9 months  =  252 real hours (10 days and 12 hours)
</pre>
<p>So in one real year about 35 Valhalla years pass. The <a cmd='#'>time</a> command 
tells you the hour, the day and the date in Valhalla. The hour of the day 
matters: the sun rises and sets, some spells work only by day, and your 
character ages with every year (see <a cmd='#'>Help Age</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Time</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Weather</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Age</a>
</pre>




</div>